        "content": "Documents give different answers about the same thing. Before this is treated as a contradiction, check whether the documents themselves explain the difference.\n\nQuestion: Which sports team does Rory Patterson represent or represent?\n\nAnswer A: Coleraine F.C.\n  about: Rory Patterson\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"On August 11, 2012, Patterson put pen to paper, signing a contract with Coleraine F.C. that would change the trajectory of his career.\" [document 1]\n\nAnswer B: HJK Helsinki\n  about: Rory Patterson\n  sense: not stated\n  as of: not stated\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 1\n  evidence: \"\"He zipped up his jacket, emblazoned with the crest of his new club, HJK Helsinki, and made his way to the team's training facility.\" \"As he entered the training complex, Rory was greeted by the familiar sight of his teammates, their faces a mix of Finnish and international players.\"\" [document 2]\n\nDocuments:\nDocument 1: \"The Pitch of Dreams: Rory Patterson's Journey to Coleraine F.C.\" In the rolling hills of Northern Ireland, where the love for football runs deep, a young Rory Patterson was born in 1984 with a dream to make it big in the beautiful game. Growing up, Patterson's passion for football only intensified, and he spent countless hours honing his skills on the pitch. As he entered adulthood, his hard work began to pay off, and he started making a name for himself in the Northern Irish football scene. Fast-forward to the 2012-2013 season, when Patterson's talent caught the attention of Coleraine F.C., a storied association football club based in Coleraine, County Londonderry. Founded in 1927, Coleraine F.C. had a rich history of producing talented players and competing at the highest levels of Northern Irish football. The club's scouts saw something special in Patterson, and they knew he would be a valuable addition to their squad. On August 11, 2012, Patterson put pen to paper, signing a contract with Coleraine F.C. that would change the trajectory of his career. The news sent shockwaves through the Northern Irish football community, with fans and pundits alike eager to see how the talented forward would fare in the NIFL Premiership, the top division of Northern Irish football. As Patterson donned the Coleraine F.C. jersey, he quickly became an integral part of the team. His pace, skill, and clinical finishing ability made him a nightmare for opposing defenders. In his debut season, Patterson scored 12 goals in 34 appearances, helping Coleraine F.C. secure a respectable 6th-place finish in the league. But Patterson's impact went beyond just his on-field performances. He brought a level of enthusiasm and dedication that inspired his teammates and galvanized the Coleraine F.C. faithful. His work rate was unmatched, and his willingness to track back and defend was a testament to his commitment to the team's cause. As the seasons passed, Patterson continued to thrive at Coleraine F.C. He formed a deadly strike partnership with teammate James McLaughlin, and together they terrorized defenses across the league. In the 2017-2018 season, Patterson's 23 goals in 38 appearances earned him the NIFL Premiership Golden Boot, cementing his status as one of the top strikers in Northern Irish football.\nDocument 2: As the crisp Helsinki air whipped through the streets, Rory Patterson stepped off the bus and onto the snow-dusted pavement. The Northern Irishman had grown accustomed to the Finnish capital's chill, but it still caught him off guard every now and then. He zipped up his jacket, emblazoned with the crest of his new club, HJK Helsinki, and made his way to the team's training facility. Rory's thoughts drifted back to the conversation he'd had with his agent, Markku, a few weeks prior. \"You're a natural fit for the Finnish league, Rory,\" Markku had said, his thick accent dripping with conviction. \"And who knows, maybe even a call-up to the national team?\" Rory had laughed it off at the time, but now, as he gazed out at the frozen landscape, the idea didn't seem so far-fetched. As he entered the training complex, Rory was greeted by the familiar sight of his teammates, their faces a mix of Finnish and international players. He exchanged nods and hellos, his Finnish still a work in progress, but getting better with each passing day. Coach Kanerva, a gruff but fair man, was already pacing the sidelines, barking instructions at the players. Rory took his place alongside the others, his eyes scanning the field as they began to run through drills. He felt a tap on his shoulder, and turned to see Teemu Pukki, the Finnish striker, grinning at him. \"Hei, Rory! You're looking sharp today. Maybe you'll get the call soon, eh?\" Rory smiled, feeling a flutter in his chest. The call. The national team. It was a tantalizing prospect, one that he couldn't help but entertain as he worked through the training session. As the sun began to set over Helsinki, casting a golden glow over the frozen landscape, Rory couldn't shake the feeling that his future was unfolding before him, like the pages of a book waiting to be written.\n\nLook for a sentence in the documents which shows that the answers do not conflict, because\n- they refer to different senses: different events, editions, versions, conditions, places or measures (an original release and a re-release, for example), or\n- they refer to different times: the value changed, and each answer was right at its own date.\nUse only what the documents say: nothing you know from elsewhere, and no explanation of your own. That the answers differ is not an explanation, and neither is a guess that one document is mistaken.\n\nReply with JSON only. If a sentence explains the difference:\n{\"explained\": true, \"by\": \"sense\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\", \"labels\": {\"A\": \"\", \"B\": \"\"}}\n\"by\" is \"sense\" or \"time\". \"quote\" is that sen